meta {
  name: Get Family Attributes (Top-Level)
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/family-attributes?account_id=6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c&_page_size=5
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data: isArray
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-15 against "David's Dev Account"
  (`6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c`). New in the 2026-09-15 `openapi_pimv3.json`
  refresh -- `GET /family-attributes` is a brand-new top-level search
  endpoint over the `product_family_id`<->`attribute_id` link records
  also reachable per-family via `/product-families/{id}/attributes`
  (see "Get Family Attributes Collection.bru").

  ## Critical finding -- NOT account-scoped by default
  Calling this endpoint with **no filter at all**
  (`GET /family-attributes?_page_size=3`) returned link records from
  **other Plytix accounts entirely** (`account_id` values
  `5ee27f5db2a5094797405d9b` and `60a61a3ac87241687d4dea1b` observed in
  one response, neither of which is "David's Dev Account"). Every other
  v3 resource confirmed in this project (all of Phases 0-5, ~50+
  endpoints) is automatically scoped to the caller's own account with no
  filter needed -- this is the **first** endpoint found that leaks
  cross-tenant data by default. The same pattern was independently
  confirmed on the two other brand-new top-level search endpoints this
  session, `GET /product-relationships` and `GET /related-products` (see
  `17-Product-Relationships/`) -- three for three of the newly-added
  top-level search endpoints in this spec refresh show the same gap.
  **This should be reported to Plytix as a likely data-isolation bug**,
  not documented to customers as normal behavior -- see
  `config/api-testing.config.md`'s new quirk and open question for this
  session.

  **Workaround for safe/scoped use**: explicitly filter with
  `?account_id=<your_account_id>` (confirmed working, as this request
  does) -- every record in this account then resolves to real
  product-family/attribute pairs.

  ## Key fields
  Each record: `account_id`, `level` (`"parent_level"` / `"no_level"` /
  `null` -- seen in the raw cross-tenant sample, meaning `level` can be
  genuinely absent), `product_family_id`, `attribute_id`. Standard
  `pagination.next_page` link. No dedicated output DTO documented in the
  spec beyond the generic `SearchFamily-attributesResponse` wrapper.
}

example {
  name: Get Family Attributes - Filtered by account_id (Safe/Scoped)
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-15, filtered to "David's Dev Account" to avoid the cross-tenant leak documented above.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/family-attributes?account_id=6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c&_page_size=5
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [
            {"account_id": "6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c", "level": "parent_level", "product_family_id": "6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b186e", "attribute_id": "6a38f613c3d65a5f868b19d1"},
            {"account_id": "6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c", "level": "parent_level", "product_family_id": "6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b186f", "attribute_id": "6a38f613c3d65a5f868b19d1"},
            {"account_id": "6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c", "level": "parent_level", "product_family_id": "6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b186d", "attribute_id": "6a38f613c3d65a5f868b19d1"},
            {"account_id": "6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c", "level": "parent_level", "product_family_id": "6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b186f", "attribute_id": "6a38f613c3d65a5f868b19cd"},
            {"account_id": "6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c", "level": "parent_level", "product_family_id": "6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b186e", "attribute_id": "6a38f613c3d65a5f868b19cd"}
          ],
          "errors": [],
          "pagination": {
            "next_page": "http://pim.dev.plytix.com/api/v3/family-attributes?account_id=6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c&_page_size=5&_page=2"
          }
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: Get Family Attributes - No Filter (Cross-Tenant Data Leak, Bug)
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-15 with NO account filter applied -- documents the data-isolation gap above. account_id values here belong to other Plytix accounts, not "David's Dev Account".

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/family-attributes?_page_size=3
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [
            {"account_id": "5ee27f5db2a5094797405d9b", "level": "parent_level", "product_family_id": "62f0f4d2cc4298ab620c7db8", "attribute_id": "5f32749f722977e42213fe7f"},
            {"account_id": "5ee27f5db2a5094797405d9b", "level": "no_level", "product_family_id": "6823647b00352c0f11ace1c9", "attribute_id": "5f32749f722977e42213fe7f"},
            {"account_id": "60a61a3ac87241687d4dea1b", "level": null, "product_family_id": "634d7a6601a8c5b91c7e3c6f", "attribute_id": "60d58862be49950ef129d1a2"}
          ],
          "errors": [],
          "pagination": {
            "next_page": "http://pim.dev.plytix.com/api/v3/family-attributes?_page_size=3&_page=2"
          }
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
